  "title": "# Build: browser-automation (Current profile) - Automated Browser plugin ## What Brett said (verbat…",
  "asked": "# Build: browser-automation (Current profile) - Automated Browser plugin ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 3 2026, voice) \"Make me a plugin that shows a browser that can be driven by the app, give it the ability to be automated and to record automation routines through the browser, like make it record in real time what you do and save the events, so you can redo everything that you just recorded, and have a powerful editor to see what each step is doing. Make it so that you can create workflows through the automated browser and record the steps, or do them automatically and record as you go, or record manually, and full powerful editing, able to tweak the JavaScript and whatever you gotta do to make it follow a routine, like go to a site and log in, or go to a site and go to a products page and grab something, and then have a scheduler built into it that you can schedule when to perform these routines.\" Book to a free named agent (Polo if his card exists, else Snap Sully). Register id `browser-automation` in the `current` profile + banner entry + What Brett said block. Work in steps through the store; each step finished and working before the next. ## Architecture (decided) - The browser runs **on the VPS** (Playwright + headless Chromium in its own container/service, persisted profile dir per workspace), because a web page can't drive other sites in an iframe. The plugin shows a **live view** (CDP screencast over websocket) you can click/type/scroll into from phone or desktop, with URL bar, back/forward/reload, tabs, device size (phone/desktop), zoom. - Console plugin `browser` (lazy-loaded once plugin-lazy-load lands), also embeddable in Molly; the engine is a shared framework library so AmberX/Gizmo can use it later. - Everything exposed via **REST + MCP + CLI** (standing rule): open, navigate, click, type, screenshot, extract, run routine, record start/stop, list/schedule routines - so Amber, Gizmo and the crew can drive it. - **Secrets**: logins use credentials from the secure vault (axHub vault / Voice Vault), referenced by name in steps (`{{vault:site-login}}`), never stored in routine files or logs; password fields masked in recordings and screenshots. ## Steps - s1 **Browser + live view + drive**: service, container, websocket screencast, input forwarding, tabs, downloads, health check in Systems check. - s2 **Recorder**: record what Brett does in real time (navigate, click, type, select, scroll, wait, file upload) as steps with robust selectors (role/text/test-id first, CSS fallback, multiple candidates) + a thumbnail per step. Three modes: Record manually, Auto (Amber/Gizmo drives via MCP) and record as it goes, and Hand-build steps. Replay with step-by-step / run all / run from here, highlight current step in the live view. - s3 **Routine editor** (`routine@1` asset, hot-swappable, shareable): step list with type, target, value, wait, retries, timeout, screenshot; edit/reorder/disable/duplicate steps; variables and loops/conditions (if element exists, for each item); **Extract** steps (text, attribute, table, list -> JSON/CSV) for 'go to products page and grab something'; per-step and whole-routine **JavaScript editor** (syntax highlight, run-in-page, console output); selector picker (tap an element in the live view); test run with per-step pass/fail and diff of results. - s4 **Scheduler**: run routines on a schedule (once, every N minutes/hours, daily/weekly at a time, cron advanced), timezone America/New_York default, enable/pause, run now, run history with logs/screenshots/extracted data, retries on failure, notify via push/banner on fail or on result, max concurrent runs, budget/time limits. Uses the framework work scheduler contract. - s5 Examples: 'Log in to a site' and 'Grab a product's price' starter routines (against a public test site, e.g. books.toscrape.com). - Each step: tests/type-check, phone + desktop screenshots, UI Review item. Report `_claude/builds/reports/browser-automation.md` (done, left, co…",
